+<dialog class="portal-guide" id="portalGuide" aria-labelledby="portalGuideTitle">
+  <div class="guide-head"><h2 id="portalGuideTitle">Portal Guide</h2><button type="button" class="guide-close" id="portalGuideClose" autofocus>Close</button></div>
+  <div class="guide-body">
+    <p>Your monthly check-in for delivery status, early delivery opportunities, and additional capacity. Your link shows campaigns assigned to your company, using the latest published Syndication Delivery source.</p>
+    <details open><summary>Complete your monthly check-in</summary>
+      <ol>
+        <li>Check the month displayed and review every campaign. <strong>Current booked volume</strong> is your publisher allocation. <strong>Current Delivered</strong> counts all valid leads, including those not yet delivered to the client.</li>
+        <li>Enter frontload and incremental volumes where requested. Use whole numbers; enter <strong>0</strong> if none. For incremental volume, you can also select <strong>No additional capacity for this campaign</strong>.</li>
+        <li>Answer each <strong>On Track to Fulfill</strong> question shown. Select <strong>No</strong> if delivery is at risk and explain the reason.</li>
+        <li>Use <strong>Vendor Notes</strong> for timing, GEO or segment restrictions, dependencies, or other context.</li>
+        <li>Click <strong>Submit Monthly Capacity</strong> and wait for the saved confirmation. This submits <strong>all campaigns together</strong>.</li>
+      </ol>
+    </details>
+    <details><summary>Frontload vs. incremental volume</summary>
+      <p><strong>Frontload:</strong> leads from your existing booked allocation that you can deliver earlier, within the displayed month. Your total booking stays the same.</p>
+      <p><strong>Example:</strong> with 1,000 leads booked, delivering 200 of those leads earlier means entering <strong>200</strong> as frontload volume.</p>
+      <p><strong>Incremental:</strong> extra leads beyond your existing booked allocation. If you can support 1,200 against a booking of 1,000, enter <strong>200</strong> as additional capacity.</p>
+    </details>
+    <details><summary>Why questions vary by campaign</summary>
+      <ul>
+        <li><strong>Frontload</strong> is unavailable for single-month campaigns, campaigns in their final month, strict allocation campaigns, or fully fulfilled campaigns.</li>
+        <li><strong>Incremental Opportunity</strong> is unavailable for campaigns already identified as Incremental or Incre.</li>
+        <li><strong>Fulfillment checks</strong> appear for unfinished single-month or final-month campaigns, and unfinished campaigns with strict allocation requirements. Answer the allocation or end-date question displayed.</li>
+      </ul>
+    </details>
+    <details><summary>Revise a saved response</summary>
+      <p>Return to the <strong>same vendor link</strong> during the month, edit your response, and click <strong>Submit Monthly Capacity</strong> again. Your latest saved response is used for Avani’s review. Changes are not saved until you submit.</p>
+      <p>If campaign assignments changed while the page was open, refresh the portal, review the current campaigns, and submit again.</p>
+    </details>
+    <div class="guide-reminder"><strong>Incremental capacity requires Avani’s confirmation and client approval before a new campaign can be built.</strong></div>
+  </div>
+</dialog>
+<script id="portalGuideScript">
+(() => {
+  const guide = document.getElementById('portalGuide');
+  const open = document.getElementById('portalGuideOpen');
+  const close = document.getElementById('portalGuideClose');
+  let previousOverflow = '';
+  open.addEventListener('click', () => {
+    if (guide.open) return;
+    previousOverflow = document.body.style.overflow;
+    guide.showModal();
+    document.body.style.overflow = 'hidden';
+  });
+  close.addEventListener('click', () => guide.close());
+  guide.addEventListener('close', () => {
+    document.body.style.overflow = previousOverflow;
+    open.focus();
+  });
+})();
+</script>
